🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- a pointer-element array field (`rizz *ptrs[2];`),
🚽 the PR's own claimed scope. Confirms storage and layout (2 pointers =
🚽 16 bytes) and that each slot independently holds the address it was
🚽 given (compared against the source variable's own `&`, not against
🚽 each other -- comparing two struct-array-field-element expressions to
🚽 EACH OTHER in one binary operation hits issue #192, a pre-existing,
🚽 unrelated bug this fixture deliberately does not exercise: confirmed
🚽 by reproducing #192 with a plain non-array scalar field and zero
🚽 array_access grammar involved at all).
🚽
🚽 Full pointer *dereference* through a struct field (`*bx.ptrs[0]`) is
🚽 also out of scope here -- blocked by the pre-existing #196/#197
🚽 "chaining through a pointer field" limitation, reproduced identically
🚽 for a plain (non-array) pointer struct field.
gang Box {
    rizz *ptrs[2];
};

skibidi main {
    rizz a = 1;
    rizz b = 2;
    gang Box bx;
    bx.ptrs[0] = &a;
    bx.ptrs[1] = &b;

    edgy (bx.ptrs[0] == &a) {
        yapping("ptr0 correct");
    }
    edgy (bx.ptrs[1] == &b) {
        yapping("ptr1 correct");
    }
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(bx));
}
